    <h2>Why Use ScreenSnap?</h2>
    <p>Publishing an app requires pixel-exact screenshot dimensions for every supported device. ScreenSnap lets you select target devices, upload once, and export perfectly resized images for every required size in seconds.</p>

    <h3>Supported Sizes</h3>
    <p>ScreenSnap covers all current <strong>App Store screenshot requirements</strong> including iPhone 6.9" (1320×2868), iPhone 6.7" (1290×2796), iPhone 6.5" (1284×2778), iPad 13" (2064×2752), and all <strong>Google Play Store screenshot sizes</strong> including Phone (1080×1920), 7" Tablet (1200×1920), and 10" Tablet (1920×2560).</p>

    <h3>How It Works</h3>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Select device types</strong> — Choose from presets or pick individual devices from Apple and Google stores</li>
      <li><strong>Upload screenshots</strong> — Drag and drop or click to upload into each device row</li>
      <li><strong>Preview and adjust</strong> — See live previews, remove or replace individual slots</li>
      <li><strong>Download ZIP</strong> — Get all resized screenshots in an organized folder structure</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Privacy First</h3>
    <p>Your screenshots are processed entirely in the browser using the Canvas API. No images are uploaded to any server. Your data stays on your device.</p>
